# Implementation Plan: Markdown Parent-Child Chunking & Pipeline Ingestion for Path D RAG

## Objective
Update the ingestion pipeline (`src/ingestion/chunking.py` and `src/ingestion/pipeline.py`) so that generated `.md` transcripts and converted `.docx` / `.md` Markdown files are parsed into parent-child hierarchies using structural Markdown headings (`##` and `###` / paragraphs). The parent sections will be saved to the branch JSON parent store, and child chunks indexed into ChromaDB with rich metadata (including `parent_id`, `topic_title`, `source_file`, `branch`, and `type`), ensuring seamless integration with the existing Path D retriever (`src/retriever.py`).

---

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> - `src/retriever.py` will not be modified to guarantee backward compatibility with existing indexed files and session queries.
> - Parent dictionaries will be populated with both `content`/`parent_text` and `topic_title`/`parent_topic_title` to ensure strict compatibility with both `src/retriever.py` and UI components.
> - File uploader and document extension lists will also support direct `.md` files in addition to `.pdf`, `.docx`, and `.txt`.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Ingestion Subsystem

#### [MODIFY] [chunking.py](file:///d:/SnowWiki/src/ingestion/chunking.py)
- Implement `parse_timestamp_seconds(heading_text: str) -> tuple[str, int, str]`:
  - Use regex `r'\[(?:(\d{1,2}):)?(\d{2}):(\d{2})\]'` to extract time from headers.
  - Convert to total seconds.
  - Return `(formatted_time, total_seconds, cleaned_heading_without_brackets)`.
  - Fallback to `("N/A", 0, original_heading)` if no timestamp is found.
- Implement `process_markdown_for_parent_child(md_content: str, source_file: str, branch_name: str) -> tuple[dict, list[dict]]`:
  - **Parent Section Extraction**: Regex split `r'\n(?=#{1,2}\s+)'` to catch `##` or `#` headings.
  - **Header & Time Extraction**: Run `parse_timestamp_seconds` on the heading string to get the clean title and time data.
  - **Fallback**: If no headers exist, fall back to `"General Overview"`.
  - **Parent UUID**: Generate unique `parent_id` (e.g. `f"parent_{uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]}"`).
  - **Parent Dictionary Entry**:
    ```python
    parent_dict[parent_id] = {
        "parent_id": parent_id,
        "topic_title": clean_title,
        "parent_topic_title": clean_title,
        "parent_text": parent_section_text,
        "content": parent_section_text,
        "source": source_file,
        "source_file": source_file,
        "type": "media_markdown",
    }
    ```
  - **Child Chunking**: Split parent section text by `### ` headings or double newlines (`\n\n`).
  - **Filtering**: Discard empty or trivial child chunks (< 30 characters).
  - **Child Chunk Payload**:
    ```python
    child_chunks.append({
        "chunk_id": f"{parent_id}_child_{idx}",
        "text": child_text,
        "chunk_text": child_text,
        "metadata": {
            "parent_id": parent_id,
            "source_file": source_file,
            "source": source_file,
            "branch": branch_name,
            "type": "media_markdown",
            "section_heading": clean_title,
            "topic_title": clean_title,
            "timestamp": formatted_time,
            "timestamp_seconds": total_seconds,
            "page": "N/A",
            "media_path": source_file,
        }
    })
    ```

#### [MODIFY] [pipeline.py](file:///d:/SnowWiki/src/ingestion/pipeline.py)
- Update `process_and_ingest_files`:
  - Support `.md` in `doc_ext` (`{".pdf", ".docx", ".txt", ".md"}`).
  - When processing media files (which generate structured Markdown via `generate_rolling_markdown`) or direct `.md` files:
    - Route content through `process_markdown_for_parent_child(md_content, filename, branch_name)`.
    - Persist `parent_dict` into the branch parent store (`PARENT_STORE_DIR / f"{branch_name}.json"` via `save_parent_store`).
    - Index child chunks directly into ChromaDB collection with `ids`, `documents`, `embeddings`, and `metadatas`.
    - Populate `state["files"][filename]["topics"]` from parent titles and save file summaries as usual.
  - Retain fallback to standard document processing for PDFs/TXTs when not in Markdown format.

#### [MODIFY] [__init__.py](file:///d:/SnowWiki/src/ingestion/__init__.py)
- Export `process_markdown_for_parent_child` in `__all__`.

